<title>BELGIUM: Renault to stop making cars in Belgium.</title>
<headline>Renault to stop making cars in Belgium.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>French car maker Renault SA will stop car production in Belgium this year, Belga news agency reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>Further details were not immediately available.</p>
<p>Unions at Renault Belgium said earlier they were to meet with management about reports the factory, which is based in Vilvoorde on the edge of Brussels, was to close.</p>
<p>Belga's report could not be immediately confirmed.</p>
<p>Officials at the plant were unavailable to comment, although a union official said a news conference was scheduled for 1900 local (1800 GMT).</p>
